{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# LLM gate runs record no per-run request or tool-call counts, so the gates cannot be tuned\n\n## The gap\n\n**Nothing durably records how many model requests or tool calls a gate run consumed.** There is no\nusage log on disk, and the audit sidecar carries criteria and citations but no request/tool-call\ncounts. Established while investigating [rebar:c827-2a23-cd00-473e]: the control-group question\n\"how many of the 240 available requests did the epics that closed cleanly actually use?\" **could not\nbe answered from the store at all.**\n\n## Why this matters — it is why the same bug recurred six times\n\nThe completion gate's step budget has been raised **five times** across its history\n([rebar:c827-2a23-cd00-473e]'s history sweep), a hard tool-call cap was proposed and deferred\n([rebar:7c58-...]) then proposed and rejected ([rebar:b2bb-...]), and the verifier's own creating\nepic was force-closed citing the limitation as \"documented\". **Every one of those decisions was made\nwithout spend data**, because the data was never recorded.\n\nThe cost of that absence is measurable: answering a single question about this gate required **four\nlive instrumented runs at ~20-50 minutes each**, re-deriving numbers that should have been a query.\nAnd the tuning advice the docs give (`docs/llm-framework.md:698-704` — \"a high recursion limit means\nyou're paying for a loop, fix the loop\") is unactionable, because nothing tells an operator whether\nthey are paying for a loop or for breadth.\n\nThis is the same **\"computed then discarded\"** shape as two sibling defects: the repetition\ndiagnostic that `interpret_failure` builds and `raise_completion_workflow_failure` drops\n([rebar:c827-...]), and the deterministic child-closure proof collapsed to a boolean\n([rebar:6ec8-24c7-182b-40d0]). The value is produced and thrown away one frame from the surface.\n\n## Scope note\n\n`usage_log` machinery already exists in-tree (e.g. `usage_log.failure_usage`,\n`usage_log.capture_attempt_messages`), and `run_ctx.usage` is live inside the tool-filter predicate.\n**Establish what is already captured before adding anything** — the likely defect is that the data is\ncaptured and not persisted, in which case this is a wiring job, not new accounting. Do not build a\nsecond, parallel usage mechanism.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] every LLM gate run persists, durably and queryably: model requests consumed, tool calls\n      consumed, the applicable limits, the step name, the ticket id, and wall-clock duration\n- [ ] the FAILURE path records it too — a run that exhausts its budget or errors is exactly when the\n      numbers are needed, and is the case most likely to be missed\n- [ ] enough signal is recorded to distinguish a LOOP from genuine BREADTH after the fact without\n      re-running: at minimum the distinct-vs-total tool-call-signature counts, so the windowed\n      distinct-ratio [rebar:70bc-ab05-6d4c-45a0] establishes can be computed from the record\n- [ ] the record is reachable by an operator without instrumenting a run — state the exact command or\n      path that retrieves it, and prove it by retrieving one\n- [ ] a test pins that the counts are actually WRITTEN on both the success and the exhaustion paths,\n      with a fixture that varies which path is taken (a success-only fixture would be vacuous here)\n- [ ] no second parallel usage mechanism is introduced where the existing one can be wired\n\n## Testing\n\n    pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -n 4 --dist worksteal -q\n    make lint && make typecheck\n    # then retrieve a real recorded run and show the counts\n\n---\n\n## Fix plan (Phase 2, rebar-debug) - wire the EXISTING mechanism, add nothing parallel\n\nConfirmed root causes are in the first comment. Three surgical changes, no new sink:\n\n1. **`usage_log.record()` stops discarding.** Add an explicit second allowlist\n   `_SHAPE_FIELDS` = (`tool_calls`, `tool_calls_distinct`, `max_consecutive_repeat`,\n   `top_repeated_tool_calls`, `request_limit`, `tool_calls_limit`, `finish_reason`) written\n   **when present** in the `usage` dict, alongside the existing `_FIELDS`. An explicit\n   allowlist, not arbitrary passthrough, so the durable telemetry schema stays owned by this\n   module. Add `duration_s` and `ticket` as explicit `record()` kwargs.\n\n2. **The success path computes the same shape from the same function.** `run_messages` is\n   already populated on the SUCCESS path too (`runner.py:513/523` - `capture_attempt_messages`\n   extends the sink in its `finally`, not only on a raise). So `runner.py` feeds those messages\n   through the SAME `usage_log.failure_usage()` the failure path already uses, and merges the\n   shape into `usage` before `record_call_spend`. One computation, both paths - the \"do not\n   build a second parallel usage mechanism\" requirement discharged literally.\n\n3. **Gate runs record by default.** `record()` resolves its sink as `REBAR_USAGE_LOG`\n   (explicit, still wins) -> else, **iff `gate_context.in_gate_session()`**, the repo-local\n   `<repo_root>/.rebar/usage.jsonl` -> else no-op exactly as today. `in_gate_session()` is the\n   existing fail-closed marker every code-reading gate binds through the single chokepoint\n   `gate_source.gate_read_root` (`gate_source.py:110`), so it is a precise \"this is a gate run\"\n   predicate and needs no new plumbing. `.rebar/*` is already gitignored and already documented\n   as the home for local rebar state. **Every non-gate caller (library consumers, spec scans,\n   unit tests) stays byte-identical**, so the module docstring's no-op-when-unset guarantee is\n   preserved for exactly the callers it was written for.\n\n### Retrieval (acceptance criterion 4)\n\n    python -m rebar.llm.usage_log summarize .rebar/usage.jsonl   # folded Markdown summary\n    cat .rebar/usage.jsonl                                       # raw per-call JSONL rows\n\n### Testing (acceptance criterion 5) - the axis that must vary\n\nA new `tests/unit/test_usage_log_run_shape_aec1.py` drives the REAL runner offline\n(`FunctionModel` + `ALLOW_MODEL_REQUESTS=False`, the established pattern in\n`test_usage_log_failed_calls.py`) and reads the FILE, across a varied path axis: `_ok_model`\n(success), `_looping_model` (budget exhaustion), and the gate-session default sink. A\nsuccess-only fixture would be vacuous here, so the exhaustion path is asserted to write the\nloop signal with its own distinct-vs-total numbers."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785947354565552001,"uuid":"d868cf94-6c39-4388-9dc9-a602223b897f"}